## Edge cases

- `COLLECT_FAILURE_COUNT=0` initialization pin must be the exact string (not just substring with nonzero suffix).
- Regional slice assertions in `test_plan_review.py` must target the round-summary writer and collector-counting blocks, not merely body-wide `COLLECT_FAILURE_COUNT` presence.
- The `resolve_collector_stderr_tail_file` removal must not affect the live `-retry.txt.stderr-tail` path.
- `parse-rate-check` requires `--id-grammar finding-oos` (not `FINDING`). `--voter-tool` is required in both tally branches.
- Legacy non-three-slot loop must omit `--slot` to avoid `set -u` abort on unset `slot`.
- The Makefile rename must update `.PHONY` and every shard reference; `test-harnesses-19` is the only shard that references `test-dispatch-code-voters-retry-claude`.
- `docs/linting.md` shard attribution must match `Makefile` (`test-harnesses-19`, not `test-harnesses-20`).

## Failure modes

- If the embedded `plan-review-loop.sh` function names differ from `_write_round_summary`, fall back to block slicing anchored on `round-summary.env` and `COLLECT_FAILURE_COUNT` co-occurrence within 40 lines.
- If legacy-branch `--voter-tool` derivation from basename is ambiguous for multi-tool panels, use a local index loop (`for i in "${!VOTER_FILES[@]}"`) with `"${VOTER_TOOLS[$i]:-claude}"` when tools are present, else basename-derived label.
- If `scripts/test-prompt-template-invariants.sh` assertions depend on the removed Codex stub branch implicitly, the harness will fail; inspect before deleting.

